#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/1
msgid ""
"Security inside was not so tight.\n"
msgstr ""
"里面安保不算严。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/2
msgid ""
"The door to my room was locked from the outside,\n"
"of course.\n"
msgstr ""
"我房间的门从外面锁上了，\n"
"当然是这样。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/3
msgid ""
"But she took off the blindfold at bath time - so she\n"
"could wash my hair...\n"
msgstr ""
"但洗澡时她摘了眼罩，好帮我\n"
"洗头……\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/4
msgid ""
"Pretty luxurious treatment for a prisoner.\n"
msgstr ""
"对囚犯来说待遇真奢侈。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/5
msgid ""
"Wasn't it? She wouldn't undo the handcuffs, but\n"
"she washed my body for me instead.\n"
msgstr ""
"不是吗？她不肯解开手铐，但\n"
"她替我洗了身体。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/6
msgid ""
"And with such gentle care...\n"
msgstr ""
"还那么温柔……\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/7
msgid ""
"Why'd you run away? Didn't she say you could go\n"
"home in a month?\n"
msgstr ""
"你为何逃跑？她不是说一个月后\n"
"就能回家吗？\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/8
msgid ""
"If your escape attempt failed, you'd be in greater\n"
"danger than before.\n"
msgstr ""
"逃跑失败，你会比之前\n"
"更危险。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/9
msgid ""
"I was supposed to be giving a presentation\n"
msgstr ""
"我本该去做一场报告，\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/10
msgid ""
"on the distribution of Costa Rican bird species at a\n"
"conference.\n"
msgstr ""
"在会议上，关于哥斯达黎加鸟类的\n"
"分布。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/11
msgid ""
"The date was approaching quickly.\n"
msgstr ""
"日子越来越近了。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/12
msgid ""
"So I pretended I had to use the toilet and made\n"
"my escape.\n"
msgstr ""
"于是我假装要上厕所，趁机\n"
"逃跑了。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/13
msgid ""
"I found an ID card and searched everywhere for\n"
"my equipment and my tape...\n"
msgstr ""
"我找到张身份证，到处找\n"
"我的装备和磁带……\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/14
msgid ""
"But a soldier saw me. It was a miracle I managed\n"
"to get away.\n"
msgstr ""
"但一个士兵看见了我。能\n"
"逃脱真是奇迹。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/15
msgid ""
"There was no time to find the tape.\n"
msgstr ""
"没时间找磁带了。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/16
msgid ""
"I don't care about the conference. I'm lucky\n"
"enough to still be in one piece.\n"
msgstr ""
"我不在乎那个会议。我能\n"
"安然无恙就已经很幸运了。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/17
msgid ""
"You bounce back quick.\n"
msgstr ""
"你恢复得真快。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/18
msgid ""
"You don't?\n"
msgstr ""
"你不是吗？\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/19
msgid ""
"....Not sure. I try not to dwell too much on the past,\n"
"but...\n"
msgstr ""
"……不确定。我尽量不多想过去，\n"
"但……\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/20
msgid ""
"Then don't. There's no point. I'm so glad to be out\n"
"of there.\n"
msgstr ""
"那就别想。没意义。我很高兴能离开\n"
"那里。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/21
msgid ""
"I never felt safe, you know?\n"
msgstr ""
"我从没觉得安全过，你知道吗？\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/22
msgid ""
"Tell me about it.\n"
msgstr ""
"可不是嘛。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/23
msgid ""
"Well... I think she's interested in women. And I think\n"
"she took a fancy to me.\n"
msgstr ""
"嗯……我觉得她对女人感兴趣。而且我觉得\n"
"她看上了我。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/24
msgid ""
"That's, uh.... huh.\n"
msgstr ""
"那，呃…哦。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/25
msgid ""
"Besides, it's much nicer here.\n"
msgstr ""
"再说，这里好多了。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6d10/0
msgid ""
"Was it just the two women in the lab?\n"
msgstr ""
"实验室里只有你们两个女人？\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6d10/1
msgid ""
"Most of the time, oui.\n"
msgstr ""
"大多数时候，是的。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6d10/2
msgid ""
"Hmm...\n"
msgstr ""
"嗯……\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6d10/3
msgid ""
"And one of them, you only heard her voice, right?\n"
msgstr ""
"其中一位你只听到了声音，对吧？\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6d10/4
msgid ""
"Yes, that is correct. Such a wonderful voice. It\n"
"sent chills up my spine.\n"
msgstr ""
"没错。那嗓音太美了，\n"
"听得我脊背发凉。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6d10/5
msgid ""
"What was the other woman like?\n"
msgstr ""
"另一位是什么样的人？\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6d10/6
msgid ""
"Don't even think about it. She's not the slightest\n"
"interest in men.\n"
msgstr ""
"别打她主意。\n"
"她对男人毫无兴趣。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6d10/7
msgid ""
"No, it's part of my mission to...\n"
msgstr ""
"不，这是我的任务所需……\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6d10/8
msgid ""
"Only teasing. Let me think...\n"
msgstr ""
"开个玩笑。让我想想……\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6d10/9
msgid ""
"I believe she was in her 30s.\n"
msgstr ""
"我记得她三十多岁。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6d10/10
msgid ""
"Pretty, with a good sense of style, but austere in\n"
"her tastes.\n"
msgstr ""
"长得漂亮，品味不错，\n"
"但喜好很朴素。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6d10/11
msgid ""
"A very... Unusual woman.\n"
msgstr ""
"非常……特别的女人。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6d10/12
msgid ""
"And she was doing research on AI?\n"
msgstr ""
"她在做AI研究？\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6d10/13
msgid ""
"AI? So that is what she was up to.\n"
msgstr ""
"AI？原来她在做这个。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6d10/14
msgid ""
"You know, she did say something interesting:\n"
msgstr ""
"对了，她说过一句有意思的话：\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6d10/15
msgid ""
"that people should not be going into space. That it\n"
"is too dangerous.\n"
msgstr ""
"说人类不该进入太空，\n"
"那太危险了。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6d10/16
msgid ""
"Hmm, an automated control system for rockets,\n"
"then?\n"
msgstr ""
"嗯，那就是火箭的\n"
"自动控制系统？\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6d10/17
msgid ""
"She said something about wanting to \"get closer to\n"
"her dying wish.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"她说想“更靠近\n"
"她的临终遗愿”。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6d10/18
msgid ""
"I think she must have been talking about an old\n"
"lover.\n"
msgstr ""
"我想她说的是一位\n"
"旧日的恋人。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6d10/19
msgid ""
"Lover... You mean another woman?\n"
msgstr ""
"恋人……你是说另一个女人？\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6d10/20
msgid ""
"My, aren't we curious about women and other\n"
"women!\n"
msgstr ""
"哎呀，你对女人和女人\n"
"的事还真好奇！\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6d10/21
msgid ""
"You want to hear the terrible things she tried to\n"
"do to me?\n"
msgstr ""
"你想听听她对我\n"
"做过多可怕的事吗？\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6d10/22
msgid ""
"That's not what I meant...\n"
msgstr ""
"我不是那个意思……\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6d10/23
msgid ""
"It's all right, you can be honest.\n"
msgstr ""
"没关系，说实话就好。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6d10/24
msgid ""
"...You two seemed to get along awfully well\n"
"together.\n"
msgstr ""
"……你们俩看起来\n"
"相处得特别好。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6d10/25
msgid ""
"No, no, not at all.\n"
msgstr ""
"不，不，完全没有。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6d10/26
msgid ""
"I think you're hiding something.\n"
msgstr ""
"我觉得你在隐瞒什么。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6d10/27
msgid ""
"Never mind! Aren't you supposed to be looking for\n"
"the quetzal?\n"
msgstr ""
"别管了！你不是该去找\n"
"格查尔鸟吗？\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6d10/28
msgid ""
"Here, I'll demonstrate its call for you.\n"
msgstr ""
"来，我给你学一下它的叫声。\n"

#: codec/1/230/0xe6d10/29
msgid ""
"I KNEW it...\n"
msgstr ""
"我就知道……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0030_000_0
#. timeline 459..1072
#: codec/1/231/0xe75f0/0
msgid ""
"Let's go over this one more time.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们再过一遍。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0030_000_0
#. timeline 1072..2020
#: codec/1/231/0xe75f0/1
msgid ""
"First, I need an ID card to get into the lab.\n"
msgstr ""
"首先，我得有ID卡才能进实验室。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0030_000_0
#. timeline 2020..3385
#: codec/1/231/0xe75f0/2
msgid ""
"That is correct. From the outside it looks like any\n"
"other ruin.\n"
msgstr ""
"没错。从外面看，它就像任何\n"
"其他废墟一样。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0030_000_0
#. timeline 3427..4778
#: codec/1/231/0xe75f0/3
msgid ""
"But on the inside it is a state-of-the-art research\n"
"facility.\n"
msgstr ""
"但内部却是一座最先进的研究\n"
"设施。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0030_000_0
#. timeline 4806..6185
#: codec/1/231/0xe75f0/4
msgid ""
"And your ID card got taken away from you by\n"
"some guy in an orange jacket.\n"
msgstr ""
"而且你的ID卡被一个穿橙色夹克的\n"
"家伙拿走了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0030_000_0
#. timeline 6255..7314
#: codec/1/231/0xe75f0/5
msgid ""
"Exactly. I heard a quetzal singing nearby.\n"
msgstr ""
"正是。我听到附近有凤尾绿咬鹃在叫。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0030_000_0
#. timeline 7453..8164
#: codec/1/231/0xe75f0/6
msgid ""
"It has not been that long since it happened.\n"
msgstr ""
"事情发生还没过多久。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0030_000_0
#. timeline 8568..10072
#: codec/1/231/0xe75f0/7
msgid ""
"It could be tricky if he's out on patrol, but if he's a\n"
"stationary sentry...\n"
msgstr ""
"他在外巡逻可能有点麻烦，但如果是\n"
"固定哨兵……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0030_000_0
#. timeline 10114..10741
#: codec/1/231/0xe75f0/8
msgid ""
"You don't think the quetzal's moved?\n"
msgstr ""
"你觉得那只凤尾绿咬鹃没挪窝？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0030_000_0
#. timeline 10825..12441
#: codec/1/231/0xe75f0/9
msgid ""
"Its nest is probably nearby. I do not think it will go\n"
"away anytime soon.\n"
msgstr ""
"它的巢穴大概就在附近。我觉得它不会\n"
"很快离开。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0030_000_0
#. timeline 12483..13318
#: codec/1/231/0xe75f0/10
msgid ""
"Good. I'll get on looking for that soldier.\n"
msgstr ""
"好。我去找那个士兵。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0030_000_0
#. timeline 13332..14572
#: codec/1/231/0xe75f0/11
msgid ""
"If you forget what it sounds like, I'll do the call for\n"
"you again.\n"
msgstr ""
"如果你忘了它的叫声，我可以再\n"
"给你演示一遍。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0030_000_0
#. timeline 14642..15729
#: codec/1/231/0xe75f0/12
msgid ""
"Just give me a call anytime you'd like to hear it.\n"
msgstr ""
"想听随时呼我。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0030_000_0
#. timeline 16049..16425
#: codec/1/231/0xe75f0/13
msgid ""
"I'll do that.\n"
msgstr ""
"我会的。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0090_000_0
#. timeline 459..1866
#: codec/1/231/0xe7ae0/0
msgid ""
"Let me get this straight. You were in Costa Rica\n"
"as a birdwatcher?\n"
msgstr ""
"让我理清楚。你在哥斯达黎加\n"
"是作为观鸟者？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0090_000_0
#. timeline 1894..3413
#: codec/1/231/0xe7ae0/1
msgid ""
"Yes, I was. Not for pleasure, though - I am a\n"
"researcher, after all.\n"
msgstr ""
"是的。不过不是消遣，毕竟我\n"
"是个研究员。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0090_000_0
#. timeline 3496..4639
#: codec/1/231/0xe7ae0/2
msgid ""
"I am studying the distribution of Latin American\n"
"bird species.\n"
msgstr ""
"我正在研究拉丁美洲\n"
"鸟类的分布。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0090_000_0
#. timeline 4764..5614
#: codec/1/231/0xe7ae0/3
msgid ""
"With today's compact cassette tape recorders,\n"
msgstr ""
"有了如今的紧凑型盒式录音机，\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0090_000_0
#. timeline 5656..6896
#: codec/1/231/0xe7ae0/4
msgid ""
"even a woman like me can carry her recording\n"
"equipment by herself.\n"
msgstr ""
"即使像我这样的女人也能独自携带\n"
"录音设备。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0090_000_0
#. timeline 7077..7843
#: codec/1/231/0xe7ae0/5
msgid ""
"But it was a mistake to come alone.\n"
msgstr ""
"但独自前来是个错误。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0090_000_0
#. timeline 7913..9445
#: codec/1/231/0xe7ae0/6
msgid ""
"Mmm. Even so, there sure are a lot of wild birds in\n"
"Costa Rica.\n"
msgstr ""
"嗯。即便如此，哥斯达黎加的野鸟\n"
"确实很多。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0090_000_0
#. timeline 9696..10685
#: codec/1/231/0xe7ae0/7
msgid ""
"Aren't there? Over 800 different species,\n"
msgstr ""
"可不是吗？800多个不同物种，\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0090_000_0
#. timeline 10741..11925
#: codec/1/231/0xe7ae0/8
#, c-format
msgid ""
"said to be more than 10% of all living bird species\n"
"on Earth.\n"
msgstr ""
"据说超过地球上所有现存鸟类物种的\n"
"10%。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0090_000_0
#. timeline 12092..13235
#: codec/1/231/0xe7ae0/9
msgid ""
"How many can you name, Mr. Ornithologist?\n"
msgstr ""
"你能叫出多少种，鸟类学家先生？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0090_000_0
#. timeline 13332..14349
#: codec/1/231/0xe7ae0/10
msgid ""
"Hey, I was just trying not to scare you...\n"
msgstr ""
"嘿，我只是不想吓到你……\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0090_000_0
#. timeline 14391..15325
#: codec/1/231/0xe7ae0/11
msgid ""
"You should at least have a basic knowledge of\n"
"Costa Rica.\n"
msgstr ""
"你至少应该对哥斯达黎加有\n"
"基本的了解。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0090_000_0
#. timeline 15394..16648
#: codec/1/231/0xe7ae0/12
msgid ""
"How about this: I will give you a thorough\n"
"education,\n"
msgstr ""
"这样吧：我来给你好好\n"
"上一课，\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0090_000_0
#. timeline 16676..17512
#: codec/1/231/0xe7ae0/13
msgid ""
"Mr. First-Time Ornithologist.\n"
msgstr ""
"初次观鸟的先生。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0090_000_0
#. timeline 17610..19072
#: codec/1/231/0xe7ae0/14
msgid ""
"Uh, OK. Start by telling me about the quetzal.\n"
msgstr ""
"呃，好。先讲讲凤尾绿咬鹃吧。\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/0
msgid ""
"Cécile, what's that machine you said you use to\n"
"make those recordings of yours?\n"
msgstr ""
"塞西尔，你说你用来录音的那台机器是\n"
"什么来着？\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/1
msgid ""
"A cassette... something or other.\n"
msgstr ""
"卡带……什么的。\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/2
msgid ""
"A cassette recorder? Or a cassette densuke, as\n"
"they say in Japon.\n"
msgstr ""
"卡带录音机？还是日本人说的\n"
"卡带densuke？\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/3
msgid ""
"Yeah, that. What is that thing, anyway?\n"
msgstr ""
"对，就那个。那东西到底是啥？\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/4
msgid ""
"A portable recording device released last year by a\n"
"Japanese company: Sony.\n"
msgstr ""
"去年日本公司索尼发售的\n"
"便携录音设备。\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/5
msgid ""
"It uses compact cassettes, making it far lighter\n"
"than open reel machines.\n"
msgstr ""
"它用紧凑型卡带，比开盘机\n"
"轻得多。\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/6
msgid ""
"It still weighs 5 kilograms, but the exercise won't\n"
"kill me!\n"
msgstr ""
"还是有5公斤重，不过这点运动量\n"
"累不死我！\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/7
msgid ""
"Ha.\n"
msgstr ""
"哈。\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/8
msgid ""
"It's user-friendly, too.\n"
msgstr ""
"而且很好上手。\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/9
msgid ""
"All the buttons have markings on them,\n"
msgstr ""
"所有按键上都有标记，\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/10
msgid ""
"allowing you to operate it without looking at it.\n"
msgstr ""
"不用看也能操作。\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/11
msgid ""
"Can you imagine missing the shot of a lifetime\n"
"simply because you'd blinked?\n"
msgstr ""
"你能想象就因为眨了下眼\n"
"错过一生一次的镜头吗？\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/12
msgid ""
"That would be devastating.\n"
msgstr ""
"那太要命了。\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/13
msgid ""
"But where'd they come up with densuke? It sounds\n"
"like a Japanese name.\n"
msgstr ""
"可densuke这名字哪来的？听着\n"
"像日本名。\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/14
msgid ""
"Allow me to field that one.\n"
msgstr ""
"这个我来答。\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/15
#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/6
msgid ""
"Kaz?!\n"
msgstr ""
"卡兹？！\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/16
msgid ""
"Densuke's a nickname that comes from the name\n"
"of an old manga character.\n"
msgstr ""
"densuke是绰号，来自一部老漫画\n"
"角色的名字。\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/17
msgid ""
"Was he some recording nerd, too?\n"
msgstr ""
"他也是个录音宅？\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/18
msgid ""
"Don't gimme that! Recording atmospheric noises is\n"
"an exhilarating art!\n"
msgstr ""
"别这么说！录环境音可是\n"
"一门刺激的艺术！\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/19
msgid ""
"There's nothing like capturing the real world in\n"
"action on tape!\n"
msgstr ""
"把真实世界录进磁带里的感觉\n"
"无可替代！\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/20
msgid ""
"It's just like taking pictures with a camera,\n"
msgstr ""
"就跟用镜头拍照一样，\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/21
msgid ""
"only with a microphone instead of a viewfinder.\n"
msgstr ""
"只不过用麦克风代替取景器。\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/22
msgid ""
"Sure...\n"
msgstr ""
"当然\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/23
msgid ""
"Listen to a tape with your eyes closed\n"
msgstr ""
"闭上眼听磁带\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/24
msgid ""
"and the scene just bursts to life in your mind's eye.\n"
msgstr ""
"脑中的画面便鲜活起来。\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/25
msgid ""
"Tell him, Cécile.\n"
msgstr ""
"塞西尔，告诉他。\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/26
msgid ""
"Absolutely. When I listen to the sounds of birds in\n"
"my apartment,\n"
msgstr ""
"当然。当我在\n"
"公寓里聆听鸟鸣时，\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/27
msgid ""
"it's like I'm back in the forest where I recorded\n"
"them.\n"
msgstr ""
"就像回到了我录制\n"
"它们的那片森林。\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/28
msgid ""
"See, she's a Parisienne. She knows what's chic.\n"
msgstr ""
"瞧，她是巴黎人，懂什么叫格调。\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/29
msgid ""
"If you say so...\n"
msgstr ""
"你说是就是吧……\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/30
msgid ""
"What do you like to record, Monsieur Miller?\n"
msgstr ""
"米勒先生，您喜欢录什么？\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/31
msgid ""
"Me? Steam locomotives, no question.\n"
msgstr ""
"我？当然是蒸汽机车。\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/32
msgid ""
"The roar of the engine, the throaty steam whistle...\n"
"More animal than machine.\n"
msgstr ""
"引擎轰鸣，汽笛低沉……\n"
"与其说机器，不如说野兽。\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/33
msgid ""
"Mmh, don't get me started!\n"
msgstr ""
"嗯，别提了！\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/34
msgid ""
"Steam locomotives are a dying breed in Japan.\n"
msgstr ""
"蒸汽机车在日本正逐渐消失。\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/35
msgid ""
"I wouldn't mind going back for a bit and making\n"
"some new tapes while I still can.\n"
msgstr ""
"我不介意回去待一阵子，趁还来得及\n"
"录些新磁带。\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/36
msgid ""
"...You're less civilized than I thought.\n"
msgstr ""
"……你比我想的还没教养。\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/37
msgid ""
"L-LESS civilized?!\n"
msgstr ""
"没、没教养？！\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/38
msgid ""
"I detest those beasts. The noise frightens off all\n"
"the birds.\n"
msgstr ""
"我讨厌那些野兽。噪音把鸟\n"
"都吓跑了。\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/39
msgid ""
"Then there's the smoke...\n"
msgstr ""
"还有那烟……\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/40
msgid ""
"I much prefer the peace and quiet of the forest.\n"
msgstr ""
"我更喜欢森林的宁静。\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/41
msgid ""
"Cécile, wait! That... That came out wrong, I...\n"
msgstr ""
"塞西尔，等等！那……我说错话了，我……\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/42
msgid ""
"Sure it did.\n"
msgstr ""
"是啊。\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8da0/0
msgid ""
"Alright, what do you want to know about quetzals?\n"
msgstr ""
"好吧，你想了解凤尾绿咬鹃什么？\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8da0/1
msgid ""
"Hmm... Give me the basics, something that'll help\n"
"me find one.\n"
msgstr ""
"嗯……先讲点基础的，\n"
"能帮我找到它的就行。\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8da0/2
msgid ""
"OK, then. First of all, as I'm sure you remember,\n"
msgstr ""
"好。首先，你肯定记得，\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8da0/3
msgid ""
"the quetzal's wings and back are emerald green\n"
msgstr ""
"凤尾绿咬鹃的翅膀和背部是翠绿色的，\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8da0/4
msgid ""
"- a dazzling blend of viridian fading into blue.\n"
msgstr ""
"——是青绿色渐变成蓝色的炫目色泽。\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8da0/5
msgid ""
"Its belly is brilliant red, and its tail feathers are\n"
"white. Such a gorgeous bird...\n"
msgstr ""
"腹部鲜红，尾羽雪白。\n"
"真是美丽的鸟……\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8da0/6
msgid ""
"Also, the male has two long decorative feathers,\n"
"but only during breeding season.\n"
msgstr ""
"雄鸟还有两根长饰羽，\n"
"不过只在繁殖期才有。\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8da0/7
msgid ""
"Among birds, males are usually more beautiful than\n"
"females.\n"
msgstr ""
"鸟类中，雄性通常\n"
"比雌性更漂亮。\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8da0/8
msgid ""
"Like a peacock's tail.\n"
msgstr ""
"就像孔雀的尾羽。\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8da0/9
msgid ""
"Yes, just like that.\n"
msgstr ""
"对，就是这样。\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8da0/10
msgid ""
"It is interesting to note that while their bodies are\n"
"only 40 cm long,\n"
msgstr ""
"有趣的是，它们的身体\n"
"只有40厘米长，\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8da0/11
msgid ""
"many quetzals reach over a meter in length when\n"
"you include their decorative plumage.\n"
msgstr ""
"可算上装饰性的尾羽，\n"
"许多能超过一米长。\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8da0/12
msgid ""
"Quetzals typically build their nests by making holes\n"
"in dead trees with their beaks,\n"
msgstr ""
"格查尔鸟通常用喙\n"
"在枯树上啄洞筑巢，\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8da0/13
msgid ""
"about three to four meters above the ground.\n"
msgstr ""
"离地大约三到四米。\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8da0/14
msgid ""
"They're omnivorous and eat everything from nuts\n"
"to lizards.\n"
msgstr ""
"它们是杂食性的，\n"
"从坚果到蜥蜴都吃。\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8da0/15
msgid ""
"Where can I find one?\n"
msgstr ""
"在哪能找到？\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8da0/16
msgid ""
"Their habitat stretches across the entire tropical\n"
"cloud forest.\n"
msgstr ""
"它们的栖息地遍布\n"
"整片热带云雾林。\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8da0/17
msgid ""
"You may end up having to rely on its song to find\n"
"one.\n"
msgstr ""
"最后可能只能靠叫声\n"
"才能找到。\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8da0/18
msgid ""
"Good to know...\n"
msgstr ""
"知道了……\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8da0/19
msgid ""
"I will do an imitation. Listen closely!\n"
msgstr ""
"我来模仿一下。听仔细了！\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8da0/20
msgid ""
"Kyohhh, kyohhh...\n"
msgstr ""
"Kyohhh，kyohhh……\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8da0/21
msgid ""
"Not bad.\n"
msgstr ""
"不错嘛。\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8da0/22
msgid ""
"Shall I do a chicken next?\n"
"Cluck-cluck-cluck-cluck-bacaaak!\n"
msgstr ""
"要不要再来个鸡？\n"
"咯咯咯咯——咯啊！\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8da0/23
msgid ""
"No thanks. That's enough.\n"
msgstr ""
"不用了。够了。\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8da0/24
msgid ""
"Are you sure? How about a monkey?\n"
msgstr ""
"真的不要？来个猴子？\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8da0/25
msgid ""
"...Don't need that, either.\n"
msgstr ""
"……那个也不用了。\n"

#: codec/1/232/0xe8da0/26
msgid ""
"Oh. All right, then.\n"
msgstr ""
"哦。那好吧。\n"

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/0
msgid ""
"You said you could do a monkey call.\n"
msgstr ""
"你说过你会学猴子叫。\n"

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/1
msgid ""
"Yes! Want to hear it?\n"
msgstr ""
"对！想听吗？\n"

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/2
msgid ""
"Yeah, I won't be able to get it off my mind until I do.\n"
msgstr ""
"想，不听我放不下。\n"

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/3
msgid ""
"Alright. Here it is, then.\n"
msgstr ""
"好，那就来吧。\n"

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/4
msgid ""
"...That's pretty good.\n"
msgstr ""
"挺不错嘛。\n"

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/5
msgid ""
"I can do others, too. Like a sheep, a pig...\n"
msgstr ""
"我还会学别的。比如羊、猪……\n"

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/6
#: codec/1/238/0xee440/19
#: codec/2/911/0x38f200/17
msgid ""
"Yeah?\n"
msgstr ""
"是吗？\n"

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/7
msgid ""
"Wow. What about a pig?\n"
msgstr ""
"哇。猪怎么叫？\n"

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/8
msgid ""
"That's uncanny!\n"
msgstr ""
"太像了！\n"

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/9
msgid ""
"Ha ha. I can do a rabbit as well.\n"
msgstr ""
"哈哈。我还会学兔子。\n"

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/10
msgid ""
"A rabbit? Rabbits make noises?\n"
msgstr ""
"兔子？兔子会叫吗？\n"

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/11
msgid ""
"Certainly. But they're very faint,\n"
msgstr ""
"当然会。但声音很轻，\n"

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/12
msgid ""
"so perhaps only someone who has owned one\n"
"would recognize them.\n"
msgstr ""
"所以也许只有养过它们的人\n"
"才能认出它们。\n"

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/13
msgid ""
"I see. So what do they sound like?\n"
msgstr ""
"这样啊。那是什么声音？\n"

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/14
msgid ""
"Listen very carefully.\n"
msgstr ""
"仔细听。\n"

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/16
msgid ""
"Seriously? Rabbits sound like that?\n"
msgstr ""
"真的？兔子这样叫？\n"

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/17
msgid ""
"I assure you, they do. Listen again.\n"
msgstr ""
"我保证。再听。\n"

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/18
msgid ""
"Never heard a rabbit do that before.\n"
msgstr ""
"我从没听过兔子这么叫。\n"

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/19
msgid ""
"They do, I swear!\n"
msgstr ""
"真的会，我发誓！\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0110_000_0
#. timeline 459..1518
#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/0
msgid ""
"Costa Rica is the home to many hummingbirds as\n"
"well.\n"
msgstr ""
"哥斯达黎加也是许多蜂鸟的\n"
"家园。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0110_000_0
#. timeline 1518..2326
#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/1
msgid ""
"The people here call them colibri.\n"
msgstr ""
"当地人叫它们colibri。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0110_000_0
#. timeline 2354..2758
#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/2
msgid ""
"Colibri, huh...\n"
msgstr ""
"colibri啊\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0110_000_0
#. timeline 2786..4583
#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/3
msgid ""
"Hummingbirds are the world's smallest birds.\n"
"Although they can vary from species to species,\n"
msgstr ""
"蜂鸟是世界上最小的鸟。\n"
"虽然不同种类会有所差异，\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0110_000_0
#. timeline 4625..6325
#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/4
msgid ""
"most are around 10 cm in length, and the smallest\n"
"no more than five.\n"
msgstr ""
"大多数体长约10厘米，而最小的\n"
"不超过五厘米。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0110_000_0
#. timeline 6366..8052
#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/5
msgid ""
"It's amazing to think that something so small can\n"
"still be a fully developed bird.\n"
msgstr ""
"很难想象这么小的东西\n"
"竟然是一只发育完全的鸟。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0110_000_0
#. timeline 8414..9306
#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/6
msgid ""
"I'd think a bird that tiny would get mistaken for a\n"
"bug.\n"
msgstr ""
"我觉得那么小的鸟会被误认为\n"
"虫子。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0110_000_0
#. timeline 9334..10490
#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/7
msgid ""
"Actually they are often mistaken for sphinx moths.\n"
msgstr ""
"其实它们常被误认成天蛾。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0110_000_0
#. timeline 10616..11382
#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/8
msgid ""
"The little darlings feed on flower nectar,\n"
msgstr ""
"这些小可爱以花蜜为食，\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0110_000_0
#. timeline 11410..12608
#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/9
msgid ""
"and their beaks are long and thin to help them\n"
"drink up the nectar.\n"
msgstr ""
"它们的喙又长又细，帮助它们\n"
"吸食花蜜。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0110_000_0
#. timeline 12678..13695
#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/10
msgid ""
"They beat their wings far faster than any other\n"
"bird.\n"
msgstr ""
"它们振翅速度远超其他\n"
"鸟。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0110_000_0
#. timeline 13722..15157
#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/11
msgid ""
"The smallest ones over 70 times a second! Can\n"
"you imagine?\n"
msgstr ""
"最小每秒超70次！能\n"
"想象吗？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0110_000_0
#. timeline 15227..15548
#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/12
#: codec/1/251/0xfbe10/4
#: codec/1/265/0x109080/13
msgid ""
"What for?\n"
msgstr ""
"为了什么？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0110_000_0
#. timeline 15603..16467
#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/13
msgid ""
"They hover in midair while they suck their nectar.\n"
msgstr ""
"它们悬在空中吸食花蜜。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0110_000_0
#. timeline 16481..17359
#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/14
msgid ""
"They can even fly straight backwards.\n"
msgstr ""
"甚至能笔直向后飞。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0110_000_0
#. timeline 17428..18223
#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/15
msgid ""
"Hovering... like a helicopter!\n"
msgstr ""
"悬停……像直升机！\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0110_000_0
#. timeline 18236..19212
#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/16
msgid ""
"That's why Amanda and her unit called that\n"
"chopper colibri.\n"
msgstr ""
"所以阿曼达部队叫那架\n"
"直升机colibri。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0110_000_0
#. timeline 19253..20702
#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/17
msgid ""
"I think it is an insult to the birds to give their\n"
"names to weapons, don't you?\n"
msgstr ""
"我觉得拿鸟名当武器是对鸟的\n"
"侮辱，你不觉得？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0110_000_0
#. timeline 20939..21928
#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/18
msgid ""
"Don't ask me. Ask the birds how they feel about it.\n"
msgstr ""
"别问我。问鸟怎么想。\n"

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/0
msgid ""
"Have you heard of the manakins?\n"
msgstr ""
"你听说过侏儒鸟吗？\n"

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/1
msgid ""
"Never.\n"
msgstr ""
"没有。\n"

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/2
msgid ""
"Unbelievable! You came all the way to Costa Rica\n"
msgstr ""
"不会吧！你大老远跑到哥斯达黎加\n"

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/3
msgid ""
"and you've never even heard of them!?\n"
msgstr ""
"居然没听说过它们！？\n"

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/4
msgid ""
"I didn't come here to look at...\n"
msgstr ""
"我不是来观鸟的……\n"

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/5
msgid ""
"Manakins are known for their beautiful courtship\n"
"dances.\n"
msgstr ""
"侏儒鸟以其优美的求偶\n"
"舞蹈而闻名。\n"

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/6
msgid ""
"The Orange-collared Manakin is said to live on the\n"
"Pacific side,\n"
msgstr ""
"据说橙领侏儒鸟生活在\n"
"太平洋沿岸，\n"

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/7
msgid ""
"the White-bearded Manakin on the Caribbean side,\n"
msgstr ""
"白须侏儒鸟在加勒比一侧，\n"

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/8
msgid ""
"and the Long-tailed Manakin is in the central basin.\n"
msgstr ""
"长尾侏儒鸟则在中部盆地。\n"

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/9
msgid ""
"The Long-tailed Manakins are especially distinctive.\n"
msgstr ""
"长尾侏儒鸟尤其特别。\n"

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/10
msgid ""
"What's special about them?\n"
msgstr ""
"特别在哪？\n"

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/11
msgid ""
"First, each young male picks an older male to\n"
"teach him how to dance.\n"
msgstr ""
"首先，年轻雄鸟挑选年长雄鸟\n"
"教它跳舞。\n"

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/12
msgid ""
"Then teachers and pupils all get in a group and\n"
"dance for the females.\n"
msgstr ""
"然后老师和学生聚在一起\n"
"为雌鸟跳舞。\n"

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/13
msgid ""
"However, only the teachers get paired off with\n"
"females.\n"
msgstr ""
"然而，只有老师才能与\n"
"雌鸟配对。\n"

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/14
msgid ""
"The pupils practice their technique for seven years\n"
"before striking out on their own\n"
msgstr ""
"学生们练习技巧七年\n"
"后才独自闯荡\n"

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/15
msgid ""
"and finding their own pupils.\n"
msgstr ""
"并收自己的徒弟。\n"

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/16
msgid ""
"I guess it takes time to get good at anything,\n"
"whether it's dancing or soldiering.\n"
msgstr ""
"不管做什么，想精通都得花时间，\n"
"跳舞也好，当兵也好。\n"

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/17
msgid ""
"Manakins always have plenty to eat.\n"
msgstr ""
"侏儒鸟从来不愁吃。\n"

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/18
msgid ""
"Apparently that is why they have so much free\n"
"time to practice dancing.\n"
msgstr ""
"据说正因如此，它们才有大把空闲\n"
"时间练舞。\n"

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/19
msgid ""
"Unlike us, obviously...\n"
msgstr ""
"不像我们……\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0130_000_0
#. timeline 445..1852
#: codec/1/234/0xea890/0
msgid ""
"Another well-known bird of the cloud forest is the\n"
"Three-wattled Bellbird.\n"
msgstr ""
"云雾林里另一种有名的鸟是\n"
"三垂肉伞鸟。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0130_000_0
#. timeline 1894..2730
#: codec/1/234/0xea890/1
msgid ""
"Wattled? What the hell's a wattle?\n"
msgstr ""
"垂肉？什么鬼东西？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0130_000_0
#. timeline 3092..3705
#: codec/1/234/0xea890/2
msgid ""
"It is just like your beard, Snake!\n"
msgstr ""
"就像你的胡子，SNAKE！\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0130_000_0
#. timeline 3970..4931
#: codec/1/234/0xea890/4
msgid ""
"It's a piece of flesh that hangs down from its chin.\n"
msgstr ""
"就是从下巴垂下来的一块肉。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0130_000_0
#. timeline 4973..5795
#: codec/1/234/0xea890/5
msgid ""
"Kind of like whiskers, but not made of hair.\n"
msgstr ""
"有点像胡须，但不是毛长的。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0130_000_0
#. timeline 5809..6534
#: codec/1/234/0xea890/6
msgid ""
"A hanging piece of flesh?\n"
msgstr ""
"垂下来的一块肉？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0130_000_0
#. timeline 6561..7370
#: codec/1/234/0xea890/7
msgid ""
"Oui, and it only grows on males.\n"
msgstr ""
"Oui，只有雄鸟才长。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0130_000_0
#. timeline 7383..8247
#: codec/1/234/0xea890/8
msgid ""
"Nothing more important to a man than his beard.\n"
msgstr ""
"对男人来说，胡子最重要。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0130_000_0
#. timeline 8498..9348
#: codec/1/234/0xea890/9
msgid ""
"So these birds are in the cloud forest, too?\n"
msgstr ""
"那这种鸟也在云雾林里？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0130_000_0
#. timeline 9418..10281
#: codec/1/234/0xea890/10
msgid ""
"They're normally found in the lowland rain forests,\n"
msgstr ""
"它们通常生活在低地雨林，\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0130_000_0
#. timeline 10323..11661
#: codec/1/234/0xea890/11
msgid ""
"but they migrate into the highland cloud forests\n"
"during breeding season.\n"
msgstr ""
"但它们会在繁殖季节\n"
"迁徙到高地云雾林中。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0130_000_0
#. timeline 11744..13068
#: codec/1/234/0xea890/12
msgid ""
"What the Three-wattled Bellbird's best known for,\n"
"though, is its loud call.\n"
msgstr ""
"不过三垂肉伞鸟最出名的，\n"
"是它响亮的叫声。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0130_000_0
#. timeline 13179..14851
#: codec/1/234/0xea890/13
msgid ""
"It makes these metallic BONG! and DING! sounds -\n"
"hence the name \"bellbird.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"它发出金属般铛！叮！声——\n"
"“钟鸟”由此得名。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0130_000_0
#. timeline 14893..15534
#: codec/1/234/0xea890/14
msgid ""
"It hardly sounds like a bird at all.\n"
msgstr ""
"听着根本不像鸟叫。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0130_000_0
#. timeline 15575..16676
#: codec/1/234/0xea890/15
msgid ""
"Even an expert bird caller like me cannot do it\n"
"justice.\n"
msgstr ""
"就算我这样的口技专家，\n"
"也学不像。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0130_000_0
#. timeline 16815..17749
#: codec/1/234/0xea890/16
msgid ""
"Doesn't sound like I'll be mistaking it for a quetzal.\n"
msgstr ""
"看来我不会把它认成凤尾绿咬鹃。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0140_000_0
#. timeline 445..1281
#: codec/1/234/0xeae40/0
msgid ""
"Do you know the national bird of Costa Rica?\n"
msgstr ""
"你知道哥斯达黎加的国鸟吗？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0140_000_0
#. timeline 1671..2633
#: codec/1/234/0xeae40/1
msgid ""
"Honestly! And you call yourself an ornithologist?\n"
msgstr ""
"真是的！还好意思说自己是鸟类学家？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0140_000_0
#. timeline 2730..3789
#: codec/1/234/0xeae40/2
msgid ""
"The national bird of Costa Rica is the Clay-colored\n"
"Robin.\n"
msgstr ""
"哥斯达黎加的国鸟\n"
"是黏土色鸫。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0140_000_0
#. timeline 3831..4792
#: codec/1/234/0xeae40/3
msgid ""
"It's a plain-looking brown bird found throughout the\n"
"country.\n"
msgstr ""
"那是一种貌不惊人的褐色鸟，\n"
"全国各地都有。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0140_000_0
#. timeline 4834..5475
#: codec/1/234/0xeae40/4
msgid ""
"Why'd they make it the national bird, then?\n"
msgstr ""
"那为什么选它当国鸟？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0140_000_0
#. timeline 5544..6492
#: codec/1/234/0xeae40/5
msgid ""
"Aren't there all kinds of better-looking birds, like\n"
"the quetzal?\n"
msgstr ""
"不是有更好看的鸟吗，\n"
"比如凤尾绿咬鹃？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0140_000_0
#. timeline 6589..7620
#: codec/1/234/0xeae40/6
msgid ""
"The Clay-colored Robin has a most exquisite song.\n"
msgstr ""
"褐背鸲的鸣声极为美妙。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0140_000_0
#. timeline 7662..8707
#: codec/1/234/0xeae40/7
msgid ""
"And I think it is part of the Costa Rican national\n"
"character\n"
msgstr ""
"我认为这正是\n"
"哥斯达黎加国民性的一部分——\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0140_000_0
#. timeline 8707..9933
#: codec/1/234/0xeae40/8
msgid ""
"to choose a bird everyone knows and loves over\n"
"prettier ones.\n"
msgstr ""
"宁可选人人熟知的鸟，\n"
"也不要更漂亮的。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0140_000_0
#. timeline 10017..11243
#: codec/1/234/0xeae40/9
msgid ""
"Somehow these people don't strike me as being\n"
"very \"Latin.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"总觉得这些人\n"
"不太“拉丁”。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0140_000_0
#. timeline 11257..12566
#: codec/1/234/0xeae40/10
msgid ""
"Speaking as an ornithologist, I am rather happy\n"
"with their choice.\n"
msgstr ""
"作为鸟类学家，\n"
"我对他们的选择相当满意。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0140_000_0
#. timeline 12594..13318
#: codec/1/234/0xeae40/11
msgid ""
"Not all birds have to be pretty.\n"
msgstr ""
"鸟不一定要漂亮。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0140_000_0
#. timeline 13332..14990
#: codec/1/234/0xeae40/12
msgid ""
"Oh, and just so you know, the quetzal is the\n"
"national bird of Guatemala.\n"
msgstr ""
"对了，顺便一提，格查尔鸟\n"
"是危地马拉的国鸟。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0150_000_0
#. timeline 445..1351
#: codec/1/235/0xeb310/0
msgid ""
"The Scarlet Macaw and the Great Green Macaw\n"
msgstr ""
"绯红金刚鹦鹉和大绿金刚鹦鹉\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0150_000_0
#. timeline 1351..2229
#: codec/1/235/0xeb310/1
msgid ""
"are also representative birds of Costa Rica.\n"
msgstr ""
"也是哥斯达黎加的代表性鸟类。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0150_000_0
#. timeline 2368..3608
#: codec/1/235/0xeb310/2
msgid ""
"Macaws are a type of parrot... enormous, stately\n"
"birds.\n"
msgstr ""
"金刚鹦鹉是鹦鹉一种……巨大，\n"
"气派。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0150_000_0
#. timeline 3761..4931
#: codec/1/235/0xeb310/3
msgid ""
"Macaw... I think I've heard that name somewhere\n"
"before.\n"
msgstr ""
"金刚鹦鹉……这名字我好像\n"
"听过。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0150_000_0
#. timeline 5168..6144
#: codec/1/235/0xeb310/4
msgid ""
"But of course you have - you're an ornithologist,\n"
"no?\n"
msgstr ""
"当然听过，你可是鸟类学家，\n"
"不是吗？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0150_000_0
#. timeline 6171..6492
#: codec/1/235/0xeb310/5
msgid ""
"Stop it....\n"
msgstr ""
"别说了\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0150_000_0
#. timeline 6673..8122
#: codec/1/235/0xeb310/6
msgid ""
"So tell me, where do macaws live in Costa Rica\n"
"today?\n"
msgstr ""
"那你说，如今哥斯达黎加的\n"
"金刚鹦鹉住在哪？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0150_000_0
#. timeline 8192..8721
#: codec/1/235/0xeb310/7
msgid ""
"Oh c'mon now...\n"
msgstr ""
"哎呀别这样……\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0150_000_0
#. timeline 9139..9696
#: codec/1/235/0xeb310/8
msgid ""
"I am only teasing you.\n"
msgstr ""
"我只是逗你玩。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0150_000_0
#. timeline 9752..10574
#: codec/1/235/0xeb310/9
msgid ""
"Macaws live not in the cloud forests,\n"
msgstr ""
"金刚鹦鹉不住在云雾林，\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0150_000_0
#. timeline 10574..11772
#: codec/1/235/0xeb310/10
msgid ""
"but in the rain forests on the Pacific side of Costa\n"
"Rica.\n"
msgstr ""
"而是住在哥斯达黎加\n"
"太平洋一侧的雨林。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0150_000_0
#. timeline 11842..13207
#: codec/1/235/0xeb310/11
msgid ""
"In the past, they were a common sight all across\n"
"the country,\n"
msgstr ""
"过去，它们在全国各地\n"
"都很常见，\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0150_000_0
#. timeline 13249..14419
#: codec/1/235/0xeb310/12
msgid ""
"but lately the population has decreased\n"
"dramatically.\n"
msgstr ""
"但最近种群数量\n"
"急剧下降。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0150_000_0
#. timeline 14517..16384
#: codec/1/235/0xeb310/13
msgid ""
"One possible cause is the pesticides sprayed to\n"
"facilitate large-scale banana cultivation.\n"
msgstr ""
"一个可能的原因是\n"
"为大规模香蕉种植喷洒的农药。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0150_000_0
#. timeline 16467..17136
#: codec/1/235/0xeb310/14
msgid ""
"Evicted from their own land, huh.\n"
msgstr ""
"被赶出自己的土地了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0150_000_0
#. timeline 17164..18543
#: codec/1/235/0xeb310/15
msgid ""
"Thankfully, conservation efforts have been gaining\n"
"some momentum lately.\n"
msgstr ""
"所幸近来保护行动\n"
"渐有起色。\n"

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/0
msgid ""
"Never heard the name \"Cosima\" before.\n"
msgstr ""
"从没听过“科西玛”。\n"

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/1
msgid ""
"The again I don't know many people from France.\n"
"Is it a common name?\n"
msgstr ""
"再说我也不认识几个法国人。\n"
"这名字常见吗？\n"

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/2
msgid ""
"No. Not that common.\n"
msgstr ""
"不，不常见。\n"

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/3
msgid ""
"But Wagner's second wife was named Cosima\n"
"Francesca Gaetana Wagner.\n"
msgstr ""
"但瓦格纳的第二任妻子就叫科西玛\n"
"弗朗西斯卡·加埃塔娜·瓦格纳。\n"

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/5
msgid ""
"You know, \"Kojima\" is a common last name in Japan.\n"
msgstr ""
"“小岛”在日本很常见。\n"

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/7
msgid ""
"It's just funny how, you know,\n"
msgstr ""
"就是觉得挺有意思，\n"

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/8
msgid ""
"I'm part Japanese and Cécile's middle name is so\n"
"close to \"Kojima.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"我有日本血统，而塞西尔的中间名\n"
"又和“小岛”这么接近。\n"

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/9
msgid ""
"It feels like... destiny unfolding.\n"
msgstr ""
"感觉像……命运安排。\n"

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/11
msgid ""
"Oui oui! That's a beautiful name you have. Cécile\n"
"Cosima Caminades.\n"
msgstr ""
"对对！名字真美。塞西尔\n"
"科西玛·卡米纳德斯。\n"

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/12
msgid ""
"Wait a second...\n"
msgstr ""
"等等……\n"

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/13
msgid ""
"Cécile Cosima Caminades... Cosima Caminades...\n"
"Hey, that’s close to...\n"
msgstr ""
"塞西尔·科西玛·卡米纳德斯…卡米纳德斯…\n"
"嘿，这跟…很接近\n"

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/14
msgid ""
"Close to what?\n"
msgstr ""
"像什么？\n"

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/15
msgid ""
"Your name... It sounds almost like the sentence\n"
"“Kojima, kaminandesu” in Japanese.\n"
msgstr ""
"你的名字…听起来几乎就是日语里的\n"
"那句“小岛，是神啊”。\n"

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/16
msgid ""
"And what does it mean, s’il vous plait?\n"
msgstr ""
"拜托，那是什么意思？\n"

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/17
msgid ""
"Well, \"kami\" is the word for \"god\" in Japanese.\n"
msgstr ""
"嗯，\"kami\"在日语里是\"神\"的意思。\n"

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/18
msgid ""
"\"Nandesu...\" Well, it's hard to explain, but placed\n"
"after \"god\" it would turn the sentence into \"is God.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"\"Nandesu……\"这个很难解释，但放在\"神\"后面\n"
"就变成\"是神\"了。\n"

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/19
msgid ""
"Okay. So?!\n"
msgstr ""
"好。所以呢？！\n"

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/20
msgid ""
"\"Kojima is God\"... Cecile's name is a message!\n"
msgstr ""
"\"小岛是神\"…塞西尔名字是讯息！\n"

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/21
msgid ""
"I don’t believe it... Kojima is God... Kojima is God...\n"
msgstr ""
"真不敢相信…小岛是神…小岛是神…\n"

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/22
msgid ""
"Umm, Kaz...?\n"
msgstr ""
"呃，卡兹……？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0080_000_0
#. timeline 404..1142
#: codec/1/235/0xebf60/0
msgid ""
"How are you enjoying Mother Base so far?\n"
msgstr ""
"母基地住得还习惯吗？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0080_000_0
#. timeline 1337..1755
#: codec/1/235/0xebf60/1
msgid ""
"It is wonderful!\n"
msgstr ""
"非常棒！\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0080_000_0
#. timeline 2131..3900
#: codec/1/235/0xebf60/3
msgid ""
"I was worried someone as cultured as you would\n"
"find the plant a little uncouth.\n"
msgstr ""
"我还担心像你这样有教养的人，\n"
"会觉得这片厂区有点粗野。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0080_000_0
#. timeline 3928..6283
#: codec/1/235/0xebf60/4
msgid ""
"Uncouth?! You've got albatross, and frigatebirds,\n"
"and terns, and tropicbirds...\n"
msgstr ""
"粗野？！这里有信天翁、\n"
"军舰鸟、燕鸥和热带鸟……\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0080_000_0
#. timeline 6311..7188
#: codec/1/235/0xebf60/5
msgid ""
"Seabirds I'd never have a chance to see in France!\n"
msgstr ""
"都是我在法国无缘得见的海鸟！\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0080_000_0
#. timeline 7244..8136
#: codec/1/235/0xebf60/6
msgid ""
"...Oh, well, great.\n"
msgstr ""
"……哦，那就好。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0080_000_0
#. timeline 8164..9390
#: codec/1/235/0xebf60/7
msgid ""
"Sorry, I know I should not spend all day chasing\n"
"birds...\n"
msgstr ""
"抱歉，我知道不该\n"
"整天追着鸟跑……\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0080_000_0
#. timeline 9418..10058
#: codec/1/235/0xebf60/8
msgid ""
"is there anything I can help with?\n"
msgstr ""
"有什么我能帮上忙的吗？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0080_000_0
#. timeline 10114..11215
#: codec/1/235/0xebf60/9
msgid ""
"Appreciate the offer. But I'm not sure what I could\n"
"ask you to do...\n"
msgstr ""
"感谢你的好意。\n"
"但我不知道能请你做什么……\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0080_000_0
#. timeline 11243..12134
#: codec/1/235/0xebf60/10
msgid ""
"Well, I'm certainly not cut out to shoot a gun...\n"
msgstr ""
"我肯定不是拿枪的料……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0080_000_0
#. timeline 12190..13318
#: codec/1/235/0xebf60/11
msgid ""
"Cécile, where'd you learn to move through the\n"
"forest like that?\n"
msgstr ""
"塞西尔，你在森林里\n"
"那样移动是跟谁学的？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0080_000_0
#. timeline 13416..14099
#: codec/1/235/0xebf60/12
msgid ""
"The birds weren't scared of you at all.\n"
msgstr ""
"那些鸟一点也不怕你。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0080_000_0
#. timeline 14127..15478
#: codec/1/235/0xebf60/13
msgid ""
"Becoming one with the forest is the very essence\n"
"of birdwatching\n"
msgstr ""
"与森林融为一体，\n"
"正是观鸟的精髓——\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0080_000_0
#. timeline 15617..16899
#: codec/1/235/0xebf60/14
msgid ""
"they won't behave naturally if they sense a human\n"
"nearby.\n"
msgstr ""
"一旦察觉附近有人，\n"
"它们就不会表现得自然。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0080_000_0
#. timeline 17052..17832
#: codec/1/235/0xebf60/15
msgid ""
"And that can really affect your observations.\n"
msgstr ""
"这会大大影响观察结果。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0080_000_0
#. timeline 17846..18724
#: codec/1/235/0xebf60/16
msgid ""
"I see... Kind of like scouting, then.\n"
msgstr ""
"我明白了……有点像侦察。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0080_000_0
#. timeline 18822..19727
#: codec/1/235/0xebf60/17
msgid ""
"I am also good at spotting birds from a distance,\n"
msgstr ""
"我还擅长远距离发现鸟，\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0080_000_0
#. timeline 19853..20716
#: codec/1/235/0xebf60/18
msgid ""
"tracking them based on the tiniest of clues,\n"
msgstr ""
"凭最细微的线索追踪它们，\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0080_000_0
#. timeline 20730..21497
#: codec/1/235/0xebf60/19
msgid ""
"and being aware of my surroundings.\n"
msgstr ""
"以及留意周围的动静。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0080_000_0
#. timeline 21538..22305
#: codec/1/235/0xebf60/20
msgid ""
"You're starting to sound even more like a scout.\n"
msgstr ""
"你听起来越来越像侦察兵了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0080_000_0
#. timeline 22319..23475
#: codec/1/235/0xebf60/21
msgid ""
"The only way to find a bird is to think like a bird.\n"
msgstr ""
"要找到鸟，就得像鸟一样思考。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0080_000_0
#. timeline 23572..24408
#: codec/1/235/0xebf60/22
msgid ""
"Now, think you can find a place for me?\n"
msgstr ""
"那么，能给我安排个位置吗？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0040_000_0
#. timeline 445..1253
#: codec/1/236/0xec6f0/0
msgid ""
"Did you live in Paris your whole life before coming\n"
"here?\n"
msgstr ""
"你来这里之前一直\n"
"住在巴黎吗？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0040_000_0
#. timeline 1434..2368
#: codec/1/236/0xec6f0/1
msgid ""
"Yes. It is my favorite city.\n"
msgstr ""
"是的。那是我最爱的城市。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0040_000_0
#. timeline 2549..3566
#: codec/1/236/0xec6f0/2
msgid ""
"Paris is the world capital of art and culture.\n"
msgstr ""
"巴黎是世界艺术与文化之都。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0040_000_0
#. timeline 3664..5489
#: codec/1/236/0xec6f0/3
msgid ""
"It has the latest fashion, the best cuisine, and the\n"
"most elegant, refined people.\n"
msgstr ""
"有最新的时尚、最好的美食，还有\n"
"最优雅精致的人。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0040_000_0
#. timeline 5614..7147
#: codec/1/236/0xec6f0/4
msgid ""
"The beauty of the Champs-Élysées at night is\n"
"almost unearthly.\n"
msgstr ""
"夜晚香榭丽舍的美\n"
"简直超凡脱俗。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0040_000_0
#. timeline 7230..8554
#: codec/1/236/0xec6f0/5
msgid ""
"The name comes from Elysium, the name of\n"
"Paradise in Greek mythology.\n"
msgstr ""
"这名字源自厄吕西翁，希腊神话中\n"
"天堂的名字。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0040_000_0
#. timeline 8721..9236
#: codec/1/236/0xec6f0/6
msgid ""
"Heaven, in other words.\n"
msgstr ""
"换言之，天国。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0040_000_0
#. timeline 9654..10755
#: codec/1/236/0xec6f0/7
msgid ""
"Must be nice for some people. Not for me.\n"
msgstr ""
"有人肯定爽。我可不然。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0040_000_0
#. timeline 10769..11674
#: codec/1/236/0xec6f0/8
msgid ""
"Are you saying the cultured life does not appeal to\n"
"you?\n"
msgstr ""
"你是说那种有文化的生活\n"
"吸引不了你？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0040_000_0
#. timeline 11688..13151
#: codec/1/236/0xec6f0/9
msgid ""
"I'm saying I never had a chance to lead one. Not\n"
"that it appealed to me anyway.\n"
msgstr ""
"我是说我从没机会过那种生活。\n"
"反正也不吸引我。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0040_000_0
#. timeline 13165..13583
#: codec/1/236/0xec6f0/10
msgid ""
"You prefer war?\n"
msgstr ""
"你更喜欢战争？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0040_000_0
#. timeline 13597..15464
#: codec/1/236/0xec6f0/11
msgid ""
"I don't... Like war. Life outside heaven just suits me\n"
"better.\n"
msgstr ""
"我不…喜欢战争。天国之外生活\n"
"更适合我。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0040_000_0
#. timeline 15492..16077
#: codec/1/236/0xec6f0/12
msgid ""
"That is a hard way to live...\n"
msgstr ""
"那种活法很艰难……\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0040_000_0
#. timeline 16119..17902
#: codec/1/236/0xec6f0/13
msgid ""
"...But if you do ever come to France, I will show\n"
"you around Paris.\n"
msgstr ""
"……不过你要是来法国，我会带你\n"
"逛逛巴黎。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0040_000_0
#. timeline 18000..19253
#: codec/1/236/0xec6f0/14
msgid ""
"Then you will see what heaven on earth is really\n"
"like.\n"
msgstr ""
"到时你就知道人间天堂\n"
"是什么样了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0050_000_0
#. timeline 459..1978
#: codec/1/236/0xecc30/0
msgid ""
"Heaven on earth, huh... The only image I have of\n"
"France is the Foreign Legion.\n"
msgstr ""
"人间天堂啊……我对法国的印象\n"
"只有外籍军团。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0050_000_0
#. timeline 2229..2995
#: codec/1/236/0xecc30/1
msgid ""
"Th-that is how you view France?!\n"
msgstr ""
"你、你对法国的印象就是这样？！\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0050_000_0
#. timeline 3037..3552
#: codec/1/236/0xecc30/2
msgid ""
"What do the French think of the them?\n"
msgstr ""
"法国人怎么看他们？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0050_000_0
#. timeline 4054..5600
#: codec/1/236/0xecc30/3
msgid ""
"It is a difficult question... We normally don't think\n"
"about it so much.\n"
msgstr ""
"这是个很难回答的问题……我们平时不会\n"
"想那么多。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0050_000_0
#. timeline 5865..7063
#: codec/1/236/0xecc30/4
msgid ""
"Critics claim it forces foreigners to take on the\n"
"most dangerous missions\n"
msgstr ""
"批评者声称，这迫使外国人承担\n"
"最危险的任务\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0050_000_0
#. timeline 7091..7732
#: codec/1/236/0xecc30/5
msgid ""
"so French citizens won't get hurt.\n"
msgstr ""
"这样法国人就不会受伤。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0050_000_0
#. timeline 7871..9445
#: codec/1/236/0xecc30/6
msgid ""
"You're right, that probably had something to do\n"
"with why it was created...\n"
msgstr ""
"你说得对，这大概和它被创立的原因\n"
"有些关系……\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0050_000_0
#. timeline 9515..10532
#: codec/1/236/0xecc30/7
msgid ""
"But I understand that along with service comes\n"
"benefits\n"
msgstr ""
"但据我所知，服役同时也有\n"
"福利\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0050_000_0
#. timeline 10532..11647
#: codec/1/236/0xecc30/8
msgid ""
"such as French citizenship and permanent\n"
"residency.\n"
msgstr ""
"比如法国公民身份和永久\n"
"居留权。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0050_000_0
#. timeline 11702..12496
#: codec/1/236/0xecc30/9
msgid ""
"Those who join are all given an equal chance,\n"
msgstr ""
"加入的人机会均等，\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0050_000_0
#. timeline 12538..14489
#: codec/1/236/0xecc30/10
msgid ""
"regardless of race, religion, education, social\n"
"status, or national origin.\n"
msgstr ""
"不论种族、宗教、教育背景、社会\n"
"地位或国籍出身。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0050_000_0
#. timeline 14558..15562
#: codec/1/236/0xecc30/11
msgid ""
"So it can be a godsend for people from poor\n"
"countries.\n"
msgstr ""
"所以对来自贫穷国家的人来说，\n"
"这可能是天赐之物。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0050_000_0
#. timeline 15993..16788
#: codec/1/236/0xecc30/12
msgid ""
"A way for the have-nots to live a decent life...\n"
msgstr ""
"是穷人过上体面生活的一条路……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0050_000_0
#. timeline 16983..17763
#: codec/1/236/0xecc30/13
msgid ""
"I guess that's not so different from MSF.\n"
msgstr ""
"我想这跟MSF也差不多。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0060_000_0
#. timeline 459..1630
#: codec/1/237/0xed150/0
msgid ""
"There's one other image I have of France: the\n"
"national anthem.\n"
msgstr ""
"我对法国还有另一个印象：\n"
"国歌。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0060_000_0
#. timeline 1643..3260
#: codec/1/237/0xed150/1
msgid ""
"Ah, La Marseillaise... Not everyone is a fan, of\n"
"course.\n"
msgstr ""
"啊，马赛曲……当然，\n"
"不是每个人都喜欢。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0060_000_0
#. timeline 3622..5057
#: codec/1/237/0xed150/2
msgid ""
"The whole \"To arms, citizens. May an impure blood\n"
"water our furrows.\" thing, eh?\n"
msgstr ""
"就是那句“武装起来，公民们。让不洁的鲜血\n"
"浇灌我们的田垄。”对吧？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0060_000_0
#. timeline 5071..6283
#: codec/1/237/0xed150/3
msgid ""
"The song was composed right after the French\n"
"Revolution.\n"
msgstr ""
"这首歌是在法国大革命\n"
"之后不久创作的。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0060_000_0
#. timeline 6352..7188
#: codec/1/237/0xed150/4
msgid ""
"Fearing what the tide of the Revolution\n"
"represented,\n"
msgstr ""
"由于害怕革命浪潮所\n"
"代表的一切，\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0060_000_0
#. timeline 7202..7941
#: codec/1/237/0xed150/5
msgid ""
"the ruling classes in neighboring countries applied\n"
msgstr ""
"对年轻的政府施加了\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0060_000_0
#. timeline 7941..8791
#: codec/1/237/0xed150/6
msgid ""
"all kinds of pressure on the young government.\n"
msgstr ""
"各种压力。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0060_000_0
#. timeline 8818..10253
#: codec/1/237/0xed150/7
msgid ""
"La Marseillaise became the anthem of the\n"
"volunteer armies that sought to protect\n"
msgstr ""
"《马赛曲》成为了那些试图保护\n"
"的志愿军的战歌\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0060_000_0
#. timeline 10267..11145
#: codec/1/237/0xed150/8
msgid ""
"constitutional rule against that pressure.\n"
msgstr ""
"宪政免受那种压力。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0060_000_0
#. timeline 11159..11911
#: codec/1/237/0xed150/9
msgid ""
"And they couldn't do that without armed force.\n"
msgstr ""
"没有武力就做不到。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0060_000_0
#. timeline 11939..13235
#: codec/1/237/0xed150/10
msgid ""
"Oui. I agree, some parts are a little belligerent,\n"
msgstr ""
"对。我同意，有些部分确实好战，\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0060_000_0
#. timeline 13291..14489
#: codec/1/237/0xed150/11
msgid ""
"but we must not forget that if it were not for\n"
"them,\n"
msgstr ""
"但我们不能忘记，如果不是\n"
"他们，\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0060_000_0
#. timeline 14558..15589
#: codec/1/237/0xed150/12
msgid ""
"France would not be the democracy it is today.\n"
msgstr ""
"法国就不会是今天的民主国家。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0220_000_0
#. timeline 445..1239
#: codec/1/237/0xed620/0
msgid ""
"Have you ever seen \"The Umbrellas of Cherbourg\"?\n"
msgstr ""
"你看过《瑟堡的雨伞》吗？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0220_000_0
#. timeline 1309..2145
#: codec/1/237/0xed620/1
msgid ""
"A movie? No, never seen it.\n"
msgstr ""
"电影？没看过。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0220_000_0
#. timeline 2173..3120
#: codec/1/237/0xed620/2
msgid ""
"No? It came out 10 years ago.\n"
msgstr ""
"不是吧？都十年了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0220_000_0
#. timeline 3650..4890
#: codec/1/237/0xed620/3
msgid ""
"Catherine Deneuve, she is so beautiful in it.\n"
msgstr ""
"凯瑟琳·德纳芙在里面太美了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0220_000_0
#. timeline 5015..6603
#: codec/1/237/0xed620/4
msgid ""
"And the music, the costumes, the colors... Oh!\n"
msgstr ""
"还有音乐、服装、色彩……啊！\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0220_000_0
#. timeline 6979..8052
#: codec/1/237/0xed620/5
msgid ""
"It takes place in the naval port of Cherbourg.\n"
msgstr ""
"故事发生在瑟堡军港。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0220_000_0
#. timeline 8094..8693
#: codec/1/237/0xed620/6
msgid ""
"That was a beachhead in Normandy.\n"
msgstr ""
"那是诺曼底登陆点。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0220_000_0
#. timeline 8735..10100
#: codec/1/237/0xed620/7
msgid ""
"It is set back when young men were conscripted to\n"
"fight in the Algerian War.\n"
msgstr ""
"背景是年轻人被征召去打\n"
"阿尔及利亚战争的年代。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0220_000_0
#. timeline 10407..11939
#: codec/1/237/0xed620/8
msgid ""
"The French government called the conflict a\n"
"\"public order operation in northern Africa.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"法国政府称这场冲突为\n"
"“北非公共秩序行动”。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0220_000_0
#. timeline 11995..12552
#: codec/1/237/0xed620/9
msgid ""
"I was still a little girl then,\n"
msgstr ""
"那时我还是个小女孩，\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0220_000_0
#. timeline 12650..14182
#: codec/1/237/0xed620/10
msgid ""
"but I can clearly remember one of my friends' older\n"
"brothers going off to fight.\n"
msgstr ""
"但我清楚记得有个朋友的哥哥\n"
"上了战场。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0220_000_0
#. timeline 14196..15185
#: codec/1/237/0xed620/11
msgid ""
"Yeah, national service is required in France.\n"
msgstr ""
"对，法国实行义务兵役制。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0220_000_0
#. timeline 15213..16021
#: codec/1/237/0xed620/12
msgid ""
"The war splits up two young lovers.\n"
msgstr ""
"战争拆散一对年轻恋人。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0220_000_0
#. timeline 16175..18083
#: codec/1/237/0xed620/13
msgid ""
"Director Jacque Demy's lyrics and Michel Legrand's\n"
"music tore at my heart.\n"
msgstr ""
"雅克·德米的词、勒格朗的\n"
"曲，撕碎我心。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0220_000_0
#. timeline 18250..19435
#: codec/1/237/0xed620/14
msgid ""
"I will never forget its wonderful melodies. Aaahh...\n"
msgstr ""
"我永远忘不了那些美妙旋律。啊啊……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0220_000_0
#. timeline 19518..19894
#: codec/1/237/0xed620/15
msgid ""
"You okay?\n"
msgstr ""
"你没事吧？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0220_000_0
#. timeline 20006..22137
#: codec/1/237/0xed620/16
msgid ""
"It changes lives - changes fates. War is not a good\n"
"thing.\n"
msgstr ""
"它改变人生，改变命运。战争不是好\n"
"东西。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0220_000_0
#. timeline 22277..23614
#: codec/1/237/0xed620/17
msgid ""
"For some reason it strikes a chord to hear that\n"
"coming from someone like you.\n"
msgstr ""
"这话从你嘴里说出来，不知为何\n"
"格外触动人心。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0230_000_0
#. timeline 459..1212
#: codec/1/237/0xedc40/0
msgid ""
"Speaking of the Algerian War of Independence,\n"
msgstr ""
"说到阿尔及利亚独立战争，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0230_000_0
#. timeline 1239..1839
#: codec/1/237/0xedc40/1
msgid ""
"you ever hear of \"The Day of the Jackal\"?\n"
msgstr ""
"你听过《豺狼的日子》吗？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0230_000_0
#. timeline 2103..3078
#: codec/1/237/0xedc40/2
msgid ""
"You mean the novel that was made into a movie\n"
"last year?\n"
msgstr ""
"你说的是去年被改编成电影的那部\n"
"小说？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0230_000_0
#. timeline 3120..4207
#: codec/1/237/0xedc40/3
msgid ""
"The OAS, a militant French underground group,\n"
msgstr ""
"OAS，法国地下激进组织，\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0230_000_0
#. timeline 4221..5907
#: codec/1/237/0xedc40/4
msgid ""
"plots to assassinate De Gaulle, hiring a hitman\n"
"known as the Jackal.\n"
msgstr ""
"密谋刺杀戴高乐，雇了个杀手\n"
"代号豺狼。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0230_000_0
#. timeline 5962..7509
#: codec/1/237/0xedc40/5
msgid ""
"Readers know that de Gaulle was not killed, but it\n"
"is still so exciting.\n"
msgstr ""
"读者都知道戴高乐没死，但读起来\n"
"还是惊心动魄。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0230_000_0
#. timeline 7551..8442
#: codec/1/237/0xedc40/6
msgid ""
"If someone was going to try to eliminate me,\n"
msgstr ""
"如果有人想消灭我，\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0230_000_0
#. timeline 8498..9334
#: codec/1/237/0xedc40/7
msgid ""
"I would hope they'd be as thorough as the Jackal.\n"
msgstr ""
"我希望他们能像豺狼一样缜密。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0230_000_0
#. timeline 9404..10685
#: codec/1/237/0xedc40/8
msgid ""
"To know everything about me without me\n"
"suspecting a thing.\n"
msgstr ""
"不让我起疑就\n"
"了解我的一切。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0230_000_0
#. timeline 10727..11006
#: codec/1/237/0xedc40/9
msgid ""
"Oh, Yeah?\n"
msgstr ""
"哦？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0230_000_0
#. timeline 11438..12260
#: codec/1/237/0xedc40/10
msgid ""
"I wonder if my birds feel the same way.\n"
msgstr ""
"不知鸟儿们也这么想？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0230_000_0
#. timeline 12288..12692
#: codec/1/237/0xedc40/11
msgid ""
"I wonder.\n"
msgstr ""
"我很好奇。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0240_000_0
#. timeline 473..2215
#: codec/1/238/0xee040/0
msgid ""
"France conducted its first successful nuclear test\n"
"in the Algerian Sahara in 1960.\n"
msgstr ""
"1960年，法国在阿尔及利亚撒哈拉\n"
"成功进行了首次核试验。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0240_000_0
#. timeline 2340..3246
#: codec/1/238/0xee040/1
msgid ""
"A lot of French scientists took part in the\n"
"Manhattan Project.\n"
msgstr ""
"许多法国科学家参与了\n"
"曼哈顿计划。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0240_000_0
#. timeline 3343..4346
#: codec/1/238/0xee040/2
msgid ""
"They defected to America to escape wartime\n"
"occupation.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们为躲避战时占领\n"
"投奔了美国。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0240_000_0
#. timeline 4416..5126
#: codec/1/238/0xee040/3
msgid ""
"Correct. And once the war was over,\n"
msgstr ""
"没错。战争结束后，\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0240_000_0
#. timeline 5154..6394
#: codec/1/238/0xee040/4
msgid ""
"they returned to France and continued their own\n"
"atomic research.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们回到法国，继续自己的\n"
"原子研究。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0240_000_0
#. timeline 6408..8317
#: codec/1/238/0xee040/5
msgid ""
"President de Gaulle did not want to have to rely\n"
"on an American nuclear umbrella for protection.\n"
msgstr ""
"戴高乐总统不愿依赖\n"
"美国的核保护伞。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0240_000_0
#. timeline 8359..9404
#: codec/1/238/0xee040/6
msgid ""
"Thus making France the world's fourth nuclear\n"
"power.\n"
msgstr ""
"法国由此成为世界第四个核\n"
"大国。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0240_000_0
#. timeline 9431..10699
#: codec/1/238/0xee040/7
msgid ""
"Some say the test's success pacified the Algerian\n"
"rebels.\n"
msgstr ""
"有人说试验成功镇住了阿尔及利亚\n"
"叛军。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0240_000_0
#. timeline 10769..11577
#: codec/1/238/0xee040/8
msgid ""
"The civil war was undoubtedly held in check.\n"
msgstr ""
"内战无疑受到了遏制。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0240_000_0
#. timeline 11633..13054
#: codec/1/238/0xee040/9
msgid ""
"But never have I equated nuclear weapons with\n"
"peace.\n"
msgstr ""
"但我从不把核武器等同于\n"
"和平。\n"

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/0
msgid ""
"France has produced many philosophers over the\n"
"years.\n"
msgstr ""
"法国多年来诞生了许多\n"
"哲学家。\n"

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/1
msgid ""
"Descartes, Bataille, Sartre, Baudrillard...\n"
msgstr ""
"笛卡尔、巴塔耶、萨特、鲍德里亚……\n"

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/2
msgid ""
"I'm familiar with Sartre myself.\n"
msgstr ""
"我本人熟悉萨特。\n"

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/3
msgid ""
"He called Che Guevara the most complete man of\n"
"the century, didn't he?\n"
msgstr ""
"他称切·格瓦拉为本世纪\n"
"最完整的人，对吧？\n"

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/4
msgid ""
"Smart guy.\n"
msgstr ""
"聪明。\n"

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/5
msgid ""
"He does tend to sympathize with the left. What\n"
"else do you know about him.\n"
msgstr ""
"他确实倾向左派。关于他\n"
"你还知道什么。\n"

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/6
msgid ""
"...That's it.\n"
msgstr ""
"……就这些。\n"

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/7
msgid ""
"You know nothing else?\n"
msgstr ""
"别的都不知道？\n"

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/8
msgid ""
"...Nope.\n"
msgstr ""
"……不知道。\n"

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/9
msgid ""
"Ooh la la. The man is one of the giants of\n"
"existentialism, you know.\n"
msgstr ""
"哎呀呀。他可是存在主义的\n"
"巨匠之一啊。\n"

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/10
msgid ""
"Exitentialism? I've been meaning to look into that.\n"
msgstr ""
"存在主义？我一直想研究一下。\n"

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/11
msgid ""
"Nothing more dangerous than sneaking in without\n"
"first securing an exit...\n"
msgstr ""
"没有什么比还没确保退路就潜入\n"
"更危险的了……\n"

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/12
msgid ""
"No, existentialism. Sometimes I wonder if my\n"
"English is not better than yours.\n"
msgstr ""
"不，是存在主义。有时我怀疑我的\n"
"英语还不如你。\n"

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/13
msgid ""
"Sorry, I'm just... not into philosophy.\n"
msgstr ""
"抱歉，我对哲学没兴趣。\n"

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/14
msgid ""
"Is that so? I would imagine it might really enrich\n"
"your life.\n"
msgstr ""
"是吗？我想那说不定真能丰富\n"
"你的人生。\n"

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/15
msgid ""
"I'd rather take action now than spend time thinking\n"
"about\n"
msgstr ""
"我宁愿现在就行动，而不是花时间思\n"
"考\n"

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/16
msgid ""
"what we are or how we're supposed to live.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们是什么，或该怎么活。\n"

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/17
msgid ""
"I guess you could say I live my philosophy.\n"
msgstr ""
"可以说我活在自己的哲学里。\n"

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/18
msgid ""
"Interesting. That sounds like something Sartre\n"
"would say.\n"
msgstr ""
"有意思。这话听着像是萨特\n"
"会说的。\n"
